section('att40-result','ATT40: earlier valid reference, 20 windows still fail','''<div class="callout"><strong>TTFT p50/p99: 2.967/5.334 seconds. All 11,842 requests succeeded.</strong> Twenty of 603 independently reconstructed trailing 20-second windows exceeded four seconds. The worst was 4.532 seconds at elapsed 573 seconds, with 394 samples. This is an improvement over ATT33, and still a strict-target failure.</div><p>The full load produced 600,333,408 input tokens and 60,802,464 uncached tokens, with 89.871884% cache hit. Net uncached work beyond the finite-cache plan was 798,080 tokens. All 42,621 full 60-second admission-window states passed the recorded 59.4–60.6M input and 5.7–6.3M uncached engineering bands. These bands are not contract tolerances or physical GPU throughput. Store recorded 47 eviction passes and 2.958 TB cumulative churn.</p><p>Generator heartbeat lag p99 was 44.320 ms; admission delay p99 36.527 ms; body-send delay p99 42.836 ms; connector waits zero. Original validity thresholds remain 50/50/100 ms. No CPU stack or locals probes were used. All 115 queue gauges drained, all collectors joined, and runtime source/container identities were rechecked. The immutable milestone contains 187 verified files, SHA256 <code>386e6f465af2b02e646fa2affcd1e72b46a976ee2a0576c8d8707e786c70dc6b</code>.</p><p>Twenty-four existing request traces show greater Prefill queueing in the late-spike selection: mean wait 1.819 seconds versus 0.479 seconds in controls. Prefill forward means were 1.091/0.992 seconds, while Decode waiting remained about 0.2 ms. The 16 hot requests and eight controls are not matched for input/cache work or randomized; overlapping stages are not additive causal contributions. These observations support testing larger chunks for Prefill queue capacity. ATT41 changes only chunk/max-prefill/matching graph sizes from 10,240 to 12,288 on the same startup-budget source. No lower-load fallback is justified yet.</p><p>ATT39's six canonical and four affinity checks were explicitly inherited on identical incarnations. A fresh cache reset and 400-request warmup preceded ATT40. Initial binding-map state was not dumped. The source and new Prefill/routing identities differ from ATT33; the performance change is observational. TPOT tail work remains deferred, and no complete TPOT certification is claimed.</p><p>'''+reportlink('20260913_121454')+''' · <a href="att40-report.md">Full result and reproduction</a> · <a href="latency-att40.json">Reconstructed latency windows</a> · <a href="att40-rolling-load-cache.json">Exact load/cache audit</a> · <a href="att40-trace-summary.json">Trace cohort summary</a> · <a href="att40-stage-cache.json">Stage/cache comparison</a> · <a href="att40-snapshot-verification.json">Immutable archive verification</a>.</p>''')
section('att41-result','ATT41: 12K chunks did not remove the spikes','''<p>All 11,842 requests completed successfully, with zero failures, empty outputs or unadmitted requests. Whole-run TTFT p50/p75/p90/p99 was <strong>3.198/3.685/4.289/5.595 seconds</strong>. Nineteen of 603 independently reconstructed Alex trailing 20-second windows reached or exceeded four seconds; the worst p50 was <strong>4.496 seconds at 446 seconds</strong>. The strict target is not met.</p><p>Generator lag p99 was 39.882 ms and the original validity checks passed. Input totaled 600,333,408 tokens, uncached 60,917,280 tokens, cache hit 89.852759%. Across 42,621 exact full 60-second admission-window states, 28 uncached states exceeded the recorded 6.3M engineering upper band, peaking at 6.318466M. These are overlapping boundary states, not 28 independent minutes. The finite-plan uncached excess was 912,896 tokens. Store recorded 47 eviction passes and 2.958 TB cumulative churn. The offered schedule was unchanged; no reduced-load fallback was used.</p><p>Only three Prefill settings changed from ATT40: chunk size, maximum Prefill tokens and matching captured graph sizes, from 10,240 to 12,288. The same eight-candidate source, images, resources, strict affinity, Store and Decode were retained. New Prefill incarnations and assignments are comparison factors. PP0 observation-time stage counters showed lower queue means but longer forward/bootstrap/handoff means on both Prefills. These stage intervals overlap and are not additive causal TTFT components. Global TTFT p50/p99 was worse than ATT40, which remains the best valid reference.</p><p>Fresh six canonical checks, four affinity checks and 400 warmup requests passed. All 115 queue gauges drained twice, collectors joined, and source/container identities were rechecked. The immutable milestone contains 249 verified files, SHA256 <code>01eed53d3efbb40ccdadb75a612315776d3eed0adafa7692aef99f25a355ea88</code>. The subsequent ATT42 8K result is recorded below and remains generator-invalid. No 6M capacity ceiling is established.</p><p>'''+reportlink('20260913_125341')+''' · <a href="att41-report.md">Full result and reproduction</a> · <a href="latency-att41.json">Reconstructed latency</a> · <a href="att41-rolling-load-cache.json">Exact load/cache audit</a> · <a href="att41-stage-cache.json">Stage comparison</a> · <a href="att41-snapshot-verification.json">Archive verification</a>.</p>''')
section('att42-result','ATT42: 8K diagnostic, generator invalid','<div class="callout"><strong>Diagnostic only: generator invalid.</strong> All 11,842 requests succeeded, with no failures, empty outputs or unadmitted requests. Generator event-loop lag p99 was 54.661 ms, above the unchanged 50 ms limit. Admission and body-send p99 were 33.709 and 41.625 ms; connector waits were zero. The unchanged validity rule prevents an accepted performance improvement.</div><p>Whole-run TTFT p50/p75/p90/p99 was <strong>2.934/3.535/4.149/5.659 seconds</strong>. Of 603 independently reconstructed Alex trailing 20-second windows, <strong>32 reached or exceeded four seconds</strong>. The worst median was <strong>4.386 seconds at elapsed 557 seconds</strong>, with 397 samples. Thus the strict target also fails independently of generator validity.</p><p>Input totaled 600,333,408 tokens, uncached 60,715,104 tokens, with 89.886436% cache hit and 710,720 net uncached tokens beyond the finite-cache plan. All 42,621 exact full 60-second admission-window states passed the recorded engineering bands. This does not override the invalid generator. Store recorded 47 eviction passes and 2.957 TB cumulative churn.</p><p>Only Prefill chunk size, maximum Prefill tokens and matching graph sizes changed from 12,288 to 8,192. The eight-candidate source and other settings were retained. PP0 observation-counter means shortened on both Prefills: forward 796/781 ms versus ATT40\'s 909/909 ms, while queue means rose to 936/796 ms versus 632/606 ms. These are observation-time cohorts, not matched requests or additive TTFT components. New Prefill identities and routing assignments are comparison factors. The subsequent ATT43 6K trial developed a sustained backlog and was stopped; see its partial result below. No 6M capacity ceiling is established.</p><p>Fresh six canonical and four affinity checks passed; 400 warmup requests completed with a valid generator. All 115 queue gauges were idle twice, collectors joined, and runtime identities and source hashes were rechecked. The immutable milestone contains 264 verified files, SHA256 <code>4940b09f741464bb9274390a17fb500f907b81272e99ded2b79d03fa015939d7</code>. A scoped memory snapshot and selected allocator startup-environment audit are preserved privately. Low NVML free memory alone does not establish allocator pressure; no allocator or logits-budget-fraction change was made. Rejection sampling remains prepared for the secondary 1P1D experiment.</p><p><a href="http://43.156.43.133:31019/replay/runs/20260913_132716/report?view=overview&amp;columns=overview">Alex report</a> · <a href="att42-report.md">Full result and reproduction</a> · <a href="latency-att42.json">Reconstructed latency</a> · <a href="att42-rolling-load-cache.json">Exact load/cache audit</a> · <a href="att42-stage-cache.json">Stage comparison</a> · <a href="att42-snapshot-verification.json">Archive verification</a>.</p>')
section('att43-result','ATT43: 6K backlog, partial negative result','''<div class="callout"><strong>The 6K trial failed the strict latency goal.</strong> The existing guard stopped admissions after frontend activity exceeded 250 and the combined Prefill queue exceeded 120 for 15 seconds. All <strong>10,140 admitted requests succeeded</strong>; 1,702 of the planned 11,842 were never admitted. There were no failures or empty outputs. The generator passed its original validity limits. Last admission was at 513.664 seconds, last completion at 529.993 seconds; this is not a full 600-second qualification.</div><p>Completed-request TTFT p50/p75/p90/p99 was <strong>5.287/7.288/11.680/16.400 seconds</strong>. All 529 Alex trailing 20-second completion windows were independently reconstructed; <strong>310 reached or exceeded four seconds</strong>. The worst median was <strong>15.653 seconds at elapsed 530 seconds</strong>, with 372 samples. That final window includes drain and remains part of the result.</p><p>Input totaled 514,010,827 tokens, uncached 51,985,355 tokens, with 89.886331% cache hit. All 35,809 complete 60-second admission-window states within the observed span passed the recorded load bands. Net finite-plan excess was 611,584 tokens. Store recorded 39 eviction passes and 2.454 TB cumulative churn. Passing partial-span load checks does not establish full-run acceptance. Shorter stage-counter means accompanied much larger queue delays; these are observational comparisons, not additive causal decompositions.</p><p><strong>Startup incident preserved:</strong> the first Prefill151 container failed an EGM allocation on PP3 before benchmark traffic, logging a CUDA memory-creation failure. Kubernetes reported the parent exit as Completed, then automatically restarted that pod once. Its second container passed fresh source, rank, graph, capacity, eight startup-budget, six canonical and four affinity checks; 400 warmup requests succeeded with a valid generator. Apply-to-ready took 706.781 seconds including the failed startup. The exact failure, one-retry intent and recovery are preserved privately. Its root cause is unproven; no manual memory reclaim, compaction or configuration change was used for recovery.</p><p>Only Prefill chunk/max-prefill/graph sizes changed to 6,144. The eight retained performance candidates and other serving settings were unchanged. All 115 queue gauges drained twice, collectors joined and source/container identities were rechecked. The immutable archive contains 276 verified files, SHA256 <code>0ca9ed7d76c3eba3da89de067fa799cf9c7b27a8f50c9e8b6f0b21b098a25906</code>. ATT40 remains the best valid reference. ATT44 returns to 10K with Prefill device-time and allocator diagnostics; both may introduce overhead and any useful optimization requires an uninstrumented confirmation. Rejection sampling remains reserved for the later 12-GPU 1P1D experiment.</p><p><a href="http://43.156.43.133:31019/replay/runs/20260913_140451/report?view=overview&amp;columns=overview">Alex report</a> · <a href="att43-report.md">Full result and reproduction</a> · <a href="latency-att43.json">Reconstructed partial latency</a> · <a href="att43-rolling-load-cache.json">Partial load/cache audit</a> · <a href="att43-stage-cache.json">Stage comparison</a> · <a href="att43-snapshot-verification.json">Archive verification</a>.</p>''')
section('att44-result','ATT44: native counters and Prefill queue spikes','<div class="callout"><strong>Diagnostic result: all 11,842 requests succeeded, but the strict TTFT target failed.</strong> Whole-run p50/p75/p90/p99 was 3.032/3.696/4.628/7.101 seconds. Of 603 independently reconstructed Alex trailing 20-second completion windows, 79 reached four seconds. The worst median was 6.187 seconds at elapsed 314 seconds, with 375 samples. ATT40 remains the best valid performance reference.</div>\n<p>The generator passed its unchanged limits: event-loop lag p99 43.526 ms, admission delay 31.621 ms, body-send delay 38.188 ms, and zero connector waits. Input totaled 600,333,408 tokens, uncached 61,003,424 tokens, with 89.838409% cache hit. Net finite-plan excess was 999,040 tokens. All 42,621 complete 60-second admission-window states were checked; 312 overlapping uncached states exceeded the recorded 6.3M engineering band, peaking at 6.341314M. These are not 312 independent minutes. Store recorded 47 eviction passes and 2.958 TB cumulative churn.</p>\n<p>All eight Prefill ranks exposed the native CUDA forward-event counters and PyTorch allocator statistics. There were five allocator retries and zero allocator OOMs during measurement; the separate warmup interval had fifteen retries. One measured retry was observed between 302 and 307 seconds, before the worst latency range. However, the later 440–458 and 497–513 second failing ranges had no new allocator retries. These sample intervals are not allocation durations, and proximity does not establish causality. Eliminating retries alone is not yet an established remedy.</p>\n<p>Twenty-four existing request traces support continued focus on Prefill queueing. Sixteen requests selected across the worst window had mean Prefill waiting 3.474 seconds, versus 0.178 seconds for eight controls. Forward means were 1.057/0.737 seconds, bootstrap 0.858/0.606 seconds and handoff 0.844/0.616 seconds. Decode waiting stayed near 0.25 ms and forward near 0.24 seconds. These selected cohorts are neither matched nor randomized; overlapping intervals cannot be added as causal TTFT components.</p>\n<p>This arm returned from 6K to 10K Prefill chunks and added the built-in device timer plus an opt-in allocator reporter. The eight performance candidates, images, Decode, frontend, Store, strict affinity, C05 workload and output20 were retained. New Prefill identities and instrumentation are comparison factors; the difference from ATT40 does not measure observer overhead alone. Forward-event spans include stream and enqueue gaps. All 115 queue gauges drained twice, collectors joined and source/container identities were rechecked. The immutable milestone contains 295 verified files, SHA256 <code>fdbbf1cc1df9548bb03ec6d352849a61e29407158408ef1506ad6130c9c55633</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Prepared only:</strong> a small MQA logits-buffer lifetime patch releases a consumed score tensor before allocating the next chunk. Forty-four CPU cases preserve outputs and show fewer simultaneous fake score buffers. Subsequent native long-context checks rejected this unconditional version before deployment. The separate preflight section records the baseline diagnosis and narrowed RAGGED-only revision; neither synthetic validation nor preparation is a serving-performance result. Rejection sampling remains prepared for the later 12-GPU real-output 1P1D experiment. No reduced-load fallback or 6M capacity ceiling is established.</p>\n<p><a href="http://43.156.43.133:31019/replay/runs/20260913_143815/report?view=overview&amp;columns=overview">Alex report</a> · <a href="att44-report.md">Full result and reproduction</a> · <a href="latency-att44.json">Reconstructed latency</a> · <a href="att44-rolling-load-cache.json">Load/cache audit</a> · <a href="att44-allocator-findings.json">Allocator findings</a> · <a href="att44-native-counters.json">Native counter windows</a> · <a href="att44-trace-summary.json">Trace summary</a> · <a href="att44-snapshot-verification.json">Archive verification</a> · <a href="prepared-only-logits-lifetime.patch">Prepared-only lifetime patch</a> · <a href="prepared-only-logits-lifetime-cpu.json">CPU validation and limitations</a>.</p>')
section('att48-result','ATT48: compact logits, spike remains','<div class="callout"><strong>Valid experiment, no strict TTFT improvement.</strong> ATT48 completed all 11,842 requests with zero failures, empty outputs or unadmitted requests. The generator and all 42,621 load/cache states passed. Whole-run TTFT p50/p75/p90/p99 was 2.887/3.383/3.909/5.469 seconds, but the strict short-window target failed.</div>\n<p>All 602 Alex trailing 20-second completion-window points were independently reconstructed. Twenty-three reached four seconds, forming one interval at elapsed 299–321 seconds. The worst median was 4.532 seconds at 307 seconds, with 385 samples. ATT47 remains the best valid reference: it had 16 failing windows and a 4.136-second worst median. Differences in Prefill incarnations, routing and cache behavior prevent isolated attribution to the compact-logits change.</p>\n<p>The added candidate stores RAGGED MQA logits relative to each request\'s KV start, reducing scratch width from the sum of contexts to the largest context when the opt-in conditions hold. GEMM bounds and final KV offsets are preserved. It passed bounded native score/index/graph checks, then six model retrieval/shared-cache checks and four affinity checks. These checks establish limited compatibility; the serving comparison did not establish a latency gain. The same nine earlier performance candidates, 10K chunks, C05, output20, Decode, frontend, Store and resources were retained.</p>\n<p>Generator lag p99 was 35.970 ms, admission delay p99 34.798 ms and body-send delay p99 44.373 ms, with zero connector waits. Measured input was 600,333,408 tokens, cached input 539,619,456 and uncached input 60,713,952, for 89.886628% cache hit. Net finite-plan uncached excess was 709,568 tokens. The maximum full-minute uncached state was 6.279534M, within the retained 6.3M engineering bound. The Store recorded 47 evictions and 2.958 TB cumulative churn at its unchanged 1300 GiB capacity.</p>\n<p>Prefill waiting increased around the spike. At 270–300 seconds, P132 mean queue time was 1.594 seconds versus 0.680 seconds at 60–90 seconds; P151 was 0.862 versus 0.325 seconds. Both remained elevated in 300–330 seconds. The shared-store hit counters do not show a large L3 read burst during those intervals. These are unmatched observation-time counters, not an additive or matched causal TTFT breakdown. No allocator-retry instrumentation was active.</p>\n<p>All 115 queue gauges were idle twice, collectors joined, and bound sources and containers were rechecked. The immutable archive contains 442 verified files, SHA256 <code>1950bfd21e9ff91c7328dc48104e9f3d62dc6bb8f321ab8d1e0bcf6eab5262e9</code>. ATT49 changes only the Prefill chunk limit, batch-token limit and graph list to 8K, retaining the ten source candidates. Its completed generator-invalid result is recorded below. No 6M capacity ceiling or lower-load fallback is established.</p>\n<p>The later 12-GPU real-output 1P1D test remains prepared. All 6,021 original HTTP bodies and planner token lengths were checked; original output policies are preserved. Its two-step topology/Decode rollout, all-rank sampling checks, guard and actual-output analysis are saved privately under <code>/mnt/HPC/tom/pd-latency-followup-20260913/secondary-1p1d-12gpu/</code>. Rejection sampling has not been activated in a serving trial.</p>\n<p><a href="http://43.156.43.133:31019/replay/runs/20260913_165356/report?view=overview&amp;columns=overview">Alex report</a> · <a href="att48-report.md">Full result and reproduction</a> · <a href="latency-att48.json">Latency reconstruction</a> · <a href="att48-rolling-load-cache.json">Load/cache audit</a> · <a href="att48-stage-cache.json">Stage/cache comparison</a> · <a href="att48-store-deltas.json">Store counters</a> · <a href="att48-complete-ten-candidate.patch">Complete ten-candidate patch</a> · <a href="att48-complete-ten-verification.json">Patch reconstruction proof</a> · <a href="att48-snapshot-verification.json">Archive verification</a>.</p>')
section('att50-result','ATT50: two small spikes at 9K','<div class="callout"><strong>Two small spikes remain; the strict target still fails.</strong> ATT50 completed all 11,842 requests with zero failures, empty outputs or unadmitted requests and a valid generator. Whole-run TTFT p50/p75/p90/p99 was 2.838/3.434/4.078/5.518 seconds. All supplied whole-run TTFT targets passed.</div>\n<p>All 603 Alex trailing 20-second completion-window points were independently reconstructed. Only elapsed 247 seconds (4.008330 seconds, 384 samples) and 437 seconds (4.011806 seconds, 374 samples) reached four seconds. These remain failures of the strict requirement to stay below four seconds throughout. The small margin does not justify rounding them into a pass.</p>\n<p>Generator lag p99 was 35.293 ms, admission delay 29.269 ms and body-send delay 36.757 ms; connector waits were zero. Original limits remain 50/50/100 ms. The workload produced 600,333,408 input tokens and 61,160,032 uncached tokens, with 89.812322% cache hit. Net excess uncached work against the finite-cache plan was 1,155,648 tokens.</p>\n<p>All 42,621 exact full-minute admission-window states were checked. Input stayed within the recorded engineering band. There were 432 overlapping uncached-load states above 6.3M, with a maximum of 6.331259M; none fell below 5.7M. These are correlated boundary states, not independent minutes or physical GPU throughput. ATT47 remains the best reference satisfying both generator and load checks. ATT50 is promising under slightly greater observed uncached work, but it is not an accepted improvement or an isolated estimate of chunk-size benefit.</p>\n<p>The only serving-setting changes from ATT49 were Prefill chunk and maximum tokens 8,192 → 9,216, plus the matching 9,216-token graph shape. All ten performance source candidates, C05, output20 and other serving resources remained. Both Prefills were replaced; the six other container identities stayed fixed. Fresh eight-rank graph and source checks, six canonical checks, four affinity checks and the separate 400-request warmup passed. Changed Prefill incarnations, routing and cache behavior limit cross-run attribution.</p>\n<p>At elapsed 420–450 seconds, observed PP0 queue means were 1.203 seconds on P132 and 1.605 seconds on P151, compared with 0.408/0.390 seconds at 60–90 seconds. Later bootstrap means were 0.639/0.662 seconds, forward 0.887/0.904 seconds and final handoff 0.698/0.701 seconds. These unmatched observation cohorts overlap and cannot be added as causal TTFT components. Store recorded 47 eviction passes and 2.958 TB cumulative churn at unchanged 1300 GiB capacity.</p>\n<p>All 115 queue gauges drained twice, every collector joined, and source/container identities were rechecked. The immutable archive contains 445 verified files, SHA256 <code>6367115b4c23beaac60410c6ccae97256d5e5d07d45ff36dca5e4884d835bbfb</code>. Client TPOT p99 was 19.270 ms; 29 requests exceeded 40 ms, 26 exceeded 80 ms, and 45 short windows had p99 above 40 ms. TPOT tail work remains deferred; no complete TPOT contract certification is claimed.</p>\n<p>Next is one uniform opt-in earlier returned-bootstrap adoption trial at 9K. CPU checks showed selection eligibility one simulated loop slot earlier; this does not establish native transport progress, KV correctness or latency benefit. Healthy metadata and guard cases passed; four synthetic failure cases retain the same failed timing assertion in baseline and candidate. Fresh model checks and a full valid replay are required. The original-output 1P4GPU/1D8GPU trial with Decode rejection sampling follows this bounded trial. No lower-load fallback or 6M capacity ceiling is established.</p>\n<p><a href="http://43.156.43.133:31019/replay/runs/20260913_180611/report?view=overview&amp;columns=overview">Alex report</a> · <a href="att50-report.md">Full result and reproduction</a> · <a href="latency-att50.json">Reconstructed latency windows</a> · <a href="att50-rolling-load-cache.json">Load/cache audit</a> · <a href="att50-stage-cache.json">Stage/cache observations</a> · <a href="att50-complete-ten-candidate.patch">Complete ten-candidate patch</a> · <a href="att50-snapshot-verification.json">Archive verification</a>.</p>')
section('att49-result','ATT49: 8K completed, generator invalid','<div class="callout"><strong>Diagnostic result; generator invalid and strict TTFT target missed.</strong> All 11,842 requests succeeded with zero failures, empty outputs or unadmitted requests. Whole-run TTFT p50/p75/p90/p99 was 2.855/3.510/4.106/5.207 seconds. Generator lag p99 was 51.598 ms, exceeding the unchanged 50 ms limit; admission and body-send p99 were 32.935 and 40.095 ms, with zero connector waits. ATT47 remains the best valid reference.</div>\n<p>All 603 Alex trailing 20-second completion windows were independently reconstructed. Nineteen reached four seconds: elapsed 132, 136–137, 436–438 and 502–514 seconds. The worst median was 4.345 seconds at 508 seconds, with 377 samples. Input totaled 600,333,408 tokens; uncached input was 60,920,224, with 89.852268% cache hit and 915,840 net extra uncached tokens versus the finite-cache plan. Six of 42,621 exact full-minute load states exceeded the recorded 6.3M uncached upper band, peaking at 6.319282M. All input-load states passed. These overlapping engineering checks do not replace generator validity.</p>\n<p>Only Prefill chunk size, maximum batch tokens and matching graph shapes changed from 10K to 8K. All ten source candidates and the C05/output20 workload were retained. During nominal 480–510 seconds, Prefill queue counter means were 1.896/1.445 seconds, forward means 0.817/0.800 seconds, bootstrap 0.599/0.576 seconds and final handoff 0.633/0.600 seconds. These are unmatched observation-time populations, not additive TTFT components. Storage-hit increments of 43,200/10,688 tokens do not establish a shared-Store read burst as the cause.</p>\n<p>Fresh six canonical checks, four affinity checks and a valid 400-request warmup passed. All 115 queue gauges were idle twice; collectors joined and bound source/container identities were rechecked. The immutable archive contains 444 verified files, SHA256 <code>b68a73001892b9b19a3f0a879f8e3443bb8d50df6c3b7a62b5172e209527c704</code>. TPOT p99 was 19.179 ms globally; no chart window had p99 above 40 ms, although 18 individual requests exceeded 80 ms. This is not complete TPOT contract certification.</p>\n<p>ATT50 selects an intermediate 9K Prefill quantum with the same ten sources and traffic. ATT49 supplies the exact current operational recipe, not a valid performance control; the original acceptance limits remain mandatory for the next run. No 6M capacity ceiling or fallback is established. The separate 12-GPU original-output 1P1D test, including rejection sampling and actual-output/counter accounting, remains prepared and has not been activated.</p>\n<p><a href="http://43.156.43.133:31019/replay/runs/20260913_172724/report?view=overview&amp;columns=overview">Alex report</a> · <a href="att49-report.md">Full result and reproduction</a> · <a href="latency-att49.json">Latency reconstruction</a> · <a href="att49-rolling-load-cache.json">Load/cache audit</a> · <a href="att49-stage-cache.json">Stage/cache comparison</a> · <a href="att49-store-deltas.json">Store counters</a> · <a href="att49-complete-ten-candidate.patch">Complete patch</a> · <a href="att49-complete-ten-verification.json">Patch reconstruction</a> · <a href="att49-snapshot-verification.json">Archive verification</a>.</p>')
section('att47-result','ATT47: best valid reference, smaller spikes remain','<div class="callout"><strong>New best valid reference; the strict target still fails.</strong> ATT47 completed all 11,842 requests with zero failures, empty outputs or unadmitted requests. Whole-run TTFT p50/p75/p90/p99 was 2.885/3.440/4.061/5.202 seconds. Every supplied whole-run TTFT target passed.</div>\n<p>All 603 Alex trailing 20-second completion-window points were independently reconstructed. Sixteen reached four seconds: elapsed 139–147 seconds and 294–300 seconds. The worst median was 4.136 seconds at 295 seconds, based on 363 samples. ATT40 had 20 failing windows and a 4.532-second worst median. Changed Prefill incarnations, routing assignments and cache misses prevent isolated attribution to the lifetime patch or removal of diagnostics.</p>\n<p>The generator passed its original limits: event-loop lag p99 43.444 ms, admission delay p99 34.146 ms, body-send delay p99 42.033 ms, and zero connector waits. The measured workload produced 600,333,408 input tokens, 539,669,248 cached tokens and 60,664,160 uncached tokens, with 89.894922% cache hit. Net finite-plan uncached excess was 659,776 tokens. All 42,621 exact full-minute admission-window states passed the recorded load/cache bands. The largest uncached state was 6.264791M, below the 6.3M engineering bound. These overlapping states are not independent minutes or physical GPU throughput.</p>\n<p>The only change from ATT46 removed the Prefill device timer, allocator-reporter flag and reporter source mount, restoring the pinned image reporter. All nine performance candidates, 10K chunks, C05, output20, frontend, Decode, Store and resources remained. The separate 400-request warmup, six canonical checks and four affinity checks passed. No additional allocator instrumentation was active, so this run does not establish an allocator-retry count.</p>\n<p>Prefill queue observations remain relevant: P151 PP0 mean queue time was 1.418 seconds in the 120–150-second observation interval, compared with 0.568 seconds at 60–90 seconds. P132 mean queue time was 1.107 seconds at 270–300 seconds, compared with 0.374 seconds at 60–90 seconds. These are unmatched observation cohorts, and overlapping stages cannot be added as causal TTFT components. Store recorded 47 eviction passes and 2.959 TB cumulative churn at its unchanged 1300 GiB capacity.</p>\n<p>All 115 queue gauges were idle twice, collectors were joined, and source/container identities were rechecked. The immutable archive contains 384 verified files, SHA256 <code>41c29d8b010cd28e0c220e7d904c70212cfbb5bf60b99662c2f880131b3e62c9</code>. A compact RAGGED MQA-logits candidate passed 24 native RAGGED cases, eight layout/score checks, four small PAGED checks and 20 graph replays. Valid scores matched bit-for-bit and tested KV-index selections matched. The first attempt declined insufficient GPU headroom before native execution; the second used another authorized idle GPU with unchanged limits. The fixed synthetic KV gather does not prove model accuracy or production BCG behavior, and the subsequent ATT48 serving result did not establish a latency improvement. <a href="compact-mqa-native-qualified.json">Native qualification and limits</a> · <a href="compact-mqa-candidate.patch">Candidate patch</a>. The later 12-GPU real-output 1P1D rejection-sampling experiment is still pending. No lower-load fallback or strict TTFT pass is claimed.</p>\n<p><a href="http://43.156.43.133:31019/replay/runs/20260913_161656/report?view=overview&amp;columns=overview">Alex report</a> · <a href="att47-report.md">Full result and reproduction</a> · <a href="latency-att47.json">Latency reconstruction</a> · <a href="att47-rolling-load-cache.json">Load/cache audit</a> · <a href="att47-stage-cache.json">Stage/cache comparison</a> · <a href="att47-store-deltas.json">Store counters</a> · <a href="att47-complete-nine-candidate.patch">Complete nine-candidate patch</a> · <a href="att47-complete-nine-verification.json">Patch verification</a> · <a href="att47-snapshot-verification.json">Archive verification</a>.</p>')
section('att46-result','ATT46: narrowed lifetime patch; generator invalid','<div class="callout"><strong>All 11,842 requests succeeded, but ATT46 is not an accepted performance run.</strong> The generator failed its original event-loop lag limit: p99 56.412 ms versus 50 ms. Admission delay p99 32.849 ms and body-send delay p99 40.822 ms passed; connector waits were zero. These limits have not been relaxed. ATT47 now provides the best valid 2P1D reference; ATT40 remains an earlier comparison.</div>\n<p>Whole-run TTFT p50/p75/p90/p99 was 2.980/3.534/4.155/5.203 seconds. All 604 Alex trailing 20-second completion-window points were independently reconstructed. Thirty-one windows reached four seconds: elapsed 440–456 and 500–513 seconds. The worst median was 4.313 seconds at 446 seconds, with 381 samples. Full-run contract percentiles passed, while the stricter requirement to keep every short-window median below four seconds did not.</p>\n<p>The full 600-second workload produced 600,333,408 input tokens and 60,851,680 uncached tokens, with 89.863686% cache hit. Net excess uncached work against the finite-cache plan was 847,296 tokens. Of 42,621 exact full-minute admission-window states, 258 overlapping states exceeded the 6.3M engineering bound, with a maximum 6.368818M. All input-load states passed. These admission-cohort checks are not physical GPU throughput or independent minutes. Store retained its 1300 GiB capacity and recorded 47 eviction passes with 2.958 TB cumulative churn.</p>\n<p>The only new performance code releases an already-consumed MQA score reference in the RAGGED path; the legacy PAGED path remains unchanged. The eight preceding candidates, 10K chunks, C05, output20, strict affinity, frontend, Decode and Store were retained. Native device timing and the opt-in allocator reporter remained enabled. The separate 400-request warmup passed with zero errors. Fresh six canonical and four affinity checks passed, including cross-Prefill L3 retrieval, within their recorded limited scope.</p>\n<p>Four measured allocator retries and zero allocator OOMs remained; the separate warmup had thirteen retries. Counter increases were observed on P132/PP1 at 0.726–5.726, 214.726–219.726 and 481.726–486.726 seconds, and P151/PP0 at 441.726–446.726 seconds. These are sampled observation intervals, not allocation durations. Temporal proximity and cross-run differences do not prove a causal latency contribution or isolated patch benefit. The narrowed source\'s native checks and the rejected earlier preflight are preserved in the following section.</p>\n<p>All 115 queue gauges were idle twice after completion, collectors were joined and source/container identities were rechecked. The immutable archive contains 442 verified files, SHA256 <code>7aa065e62f92b85e119d4d72f911bdaa9dfbe1e571d8cd59e5273027cc7da7d0</code>. ATT47 is a fresh confirmation with the same nine performance candidates and workload, removing only the extra Prefill diagnostics. No 6M capacity ceiling, reduced-load fallback, or successful real-output 12-GPU result is claimed.</p>\n<p><a href="http://43.156.43.133:31019/replay/runs/20260913_153855/report?view=overview&amp;columns=overview">Alex report</a> · <a href="att46-report.md">Full result and reproduction</a> · <a href="latency-att46.json">Latency reconstruction</a> · <a href="att46-rolling-load-cache.json">Load/cache audit</a> · <a href="att46-allocator-findings.json">Allocator observations</a> · <a href="att46-native-counters.json">Counter windows</a> · <a href="att46-stage-cache.json">Stage/cache comparison</a> · <a href="att46-complete-nine-candidate.patch">Complete nine-candidate patch</a> · <a href="att46-complete-nine-verification.json">Patch verification</a> · <a href="att46-snapshot-verification.json">Archive verification</a>.</p>')
section('lifetime-preflight','MQA lifetime: negative preflight and narrowed patch','<div class="callout"><strong>ATT45 was rejected before deployment; ATT46 uses a narrower source change.</strong> The original proposal deleted the consumed MQA score reference before the next row chunk. Its large-context PAGED test returned different selected KV indices. Repeating the unchanged baseline produced the same kind of disagreement, and repeated top-k calls on one identical retained score tensor also changed their selected sets. Repeated native GEMM scores were identical. This localizes the observed nondeterminism to the existing legacy PAGED selection path in this synthetic case; it does not certify its output or prove all differences harmless.</div>\n<p>The revised patch releases the reference only when the existing RAGGED routing offset is present. The PAGED path keeps its original operations and reference lifetime. Removing this single guarded deletion makes the entire module AST equal to the frozen baseline. No score arithmetic, indices, budgets, free-memory fraction, explicit synchronization or cache policy changes were added.</p>\n<p>The revised source passed 44 CPU loop cases, 24 small native cases and six larger RAGGED cases with key spans 131,072 and 524,288. Three CUDA-graph checks exercised 50 changed-input replays across old and new variants. Comparisons require exact selected-index multisets, preserve padding and reject substituted-index negative controls. Small query counts and synthetic metadata limit these checks: they do not prove full-model KV accuracy, production graph integration or lower serving latency. The original PAGED negative evidence remains preserved and is not converted into a pass.</p>\n<p>Candidate source SHA256: <code>182f5b863e82b3075f7ecf3dadf15047f283a967874b80be905f46a8822ce841</code>. ATT46 retains the ATT44 device timer and allocator reporter so retries can be compared; an uninstrumented confirmation is required for performance acceptance. Its first Helm attempt failed because the release Secret exceeded 1 MiB. Live worker identities, DGD specification/generation and Helm values were verified unchanged. Excluding chart tests and two files unused by templates produced a byte-identical rendered deployment; the subsequent upgrade succeeded. All excluded files remain in the private source record.</p>\n<p>A separate analysis of retained PP0 logs estimates graph-padding positions at about 1.5–2.0% of padded positions. Adding graph buckets offers limited savings in this proxy and can increase capture memory. Padded positions are not equal-cost GPU work, so this is not a throughput estimate.</p>\n<p><a href="unconditional-lifetime-preflight-rejected.json">Negative preflight decision</a> · <a href="ragged-logits-lifetime.patch">RAGGED-only patch</a> · <a href="ragged-logits-lifetime-cpu.json">CPU checks</a> · <a href="ragged-logits-lifetime-native.json">Native qualification and limits</a> · <a href="ragged-logits-lifetime-paged-preserved.json">PAGED preservation</a> · <a href="att46-chart-packaging-correction.json">Packaging correction</a> · <a href="graph-padding-opportunity.json">Padding proxy</a>.</p>')
section('startup-budget','ATT39: startup budget and bounded validation preserved','''<p>The opt-in startup hook is the eighth candidate code change, added to the seven retained changes. Both Prefills rolled; Decode, frontend and Store remained on the same container incarnations. All eight Prefill ranks reported an unset previous budget at the hook. Corresponding ranks initialized identically: PP0/PP1 to 8,910,624,522 bytes, PP2 to 7,564,414,156 bytes, and PP3 to 7,269,554,585 bytes. The getter and its 0.2 free-memory and static bounds are unchanged.</p><p>This observes early initialization on the new incarnations; it does not establish when ATT38's 88 MB budget was initialized. Applying the new PP1 budget to ATT38's captured dimensions would permit 3 splits instead of 252. That is counterfactual arithmetic, not observed batch timing or a measured speedup.</p><p>Eleven CPU checks, six canonical retrieval/L3 checks and four affinity checks passed. Cross-Prefill L3 reads reused exactly 18,048 tokens on each of four PP ranks in both directions. Warmup <code>20260913_112533</code> completed 400/400 requests without errors or empty outputs; generator lag p99 was 5.866 ms. Cold warmup TTFT p50 / p99 was 17.184 / 22.488 s. Tom paused before the measured replay. All collectors joined and 115 queue gauges drained. The 207-file immutable milestone is verified, SHA256 <code>f2654def6d2b2713e372897c8fd9777f8457863d2d48008ebb255527927e3e68</code>.</p><p>ATT40 subsequently completed a fresh cache reset, warmup and full valid measured replay on this runtime; its result is recorded above. The pause exceeded the 1,800-second idle affinity TTL, so the old warmup is preserved separately. No 600-second performance result is claimed for ATT39.</p><p>The secondary dataset audit verified every original compressed request frame: 5,806 of 5,921 measured requests specify 80,000 maximum output tokens, 26 specify 40,000, 26 specify 128,000, and 63 omit a limit. These are upper bounds, not generated lengths. Removing the replay override preserves original settings; prepared byte caches must use a distinct output-policy fingerprint.</p><p><a href="att39-warmup-report.md">Warmup-only milestone and reproduction</a> · <a href="att39-startup-budgets.json">Startup observations</a> · <a href="complete-eight-candidate.patch">Complete eight-candidate patch</a> · <a href="complete-eight-candidate-verification.json">Patch reconstruction check</a> · <a href="att39-snapshot-verification.json">Archive verification</a> · <a href="original-output-settings.json">Original output-policy audit</a>.</p>''')
section('numeric-budget','ATT38: 88 MB cached budget, 252 internal splits','''<div class="callout"><strong>Numeric evidence preserved; the remedy still needs testing.</strong> One internally coherent P151 PP1 snapshot showed 88,067,276 bytes of cached MQA logits budget. With 10,077 queries and 538,333 keys, each query row required 2,153,332 bytes. The resulting 40-row limit implied 252 internal subchunks. This is a captured split configuration, not a measured wall-time share.</div><p>Two inconsistent nonblocking snapshots were excluded. No numeric budget was captured on P132. All 24 dump children completed with no timeout; raw locals remain private because they can contain request data. Active source uses the default free-memory fraction 0.2, with no override on either Prefill. The original budget initialization time was not observed.</p><p>The owned diagnostic stopped after acquiring this evidence. All 2,715 admitted requests succeeded; 9,127 were never admitted. Worst 20s TTFT p50 was 9.071s; 70/146 windows exceeded 4s. Generator lag p99 21.383ms passed the unchanged gate. This was an instrumented partial trial, not a 600s performance pass. Cache hit 89.94455%; all 6,109 full 60s demand states inside its partial admission span passed the recorded engineering bands. Six Store evictions represented 377.56GB cumulative churn.</p><p><strong>Record finalized:</strong> 217 files, every archived entry verified, SHA256 <code>d48412d5e7081b5e4fe4762d33e1c327db9bb77e2af10d7c89584b8f9142d3ef</code>. All 115 queue gauges drained and all collectors joined. The seven previously retained serving changes were unchanged in this run.</p><p><strong>ATT39 candidate applied; bounded checks complete:</strong> one explicit Prefill-only startup hook refreshes the device budget through the original getter after graph capture, optional KV resizing and weight finalization, before request dispatch. Free-memory and static caps remain unchanged. It avoids a per-request memory query. Eleven CPU contract checks passed; a separate patch, base/source hashes, exact rendered deployment delta and rollback recipe are preserved. Six canonical and four affinity checks and400/400warmup requests passed; ATT40 subsequently completed the full valid load with improved observed TTFT and 20 failing windows, as recorded above. New Prefill identities and routing assignments are comparison factors.</p><p>'''+reportlink('20260913_104049')+''' · <a href="att38-report.md">Full result and reproduction</a> · <a href="att38-numeric-finding.json">Numeric evidence and exclusions</a> · <a href="latency-att38.json">Reconstructed chart</a> · <a href="att38-snapshot-verification.json">Archive verification</a> · <a href="startup-logits-budget.patch">Candidate source diff</a> · <a href="startup-logits-cpu-tests.json">CPU checks</a>.</p>''')
section('dsa-budget-lead','ATT37: logits splitting on Prefill 151','''<div class="callout"><strong>A concrete lead, not a demonstrated fix.</strong> The unchanged 10K repeat admitted 4,212 requests, all successful, before its backlog guard stopped the run. Worst 20s TTFT p50 was 14.229s; 166 of 227 reconstructed windows exceeded 4s. Generator lag p99 was 52.172ms, above the unchanged 50ms limit. This is an interrupted, instrumented diagnostic.</div><p>Seven of eight nonblocking CPU profiles completed. On P151 PP1, 131 of 222 main-thread samples were inside the MQA logits subchunk loop; P132 PP1 had 2 of 213. P151 PP2 and PP3 frequently sampled PP communication waits. These are conditional Python stack observations, not measured GPU durations or exact wall-time shares.</p><p>The active DSA source on both Prefills matches the preserved source. It caches a logits budget from the first non-capture free-VRAM reading and reuses that budget for later split decisions. Breakable CUDA graph batches still execute eager DSA split operations. At ATT37 closure, numeric values were unobserved. ATT38 subsequently captured the88MB budget and252split dimensions detailed above; causal benefit from a change remains unproven.</p><p><strong>Capture limitation preserved:</strong> the P151 PP0 sampler exceeded its timeout. SIGINT did not stop it; exact command and process-birth checks preceded SIGKILL of that sampler alone. No PP0 profile was recovered. The serving process was not signaled. All requests drained, all 115 queue gauges were idle, and every collector was joined.</p><p>The immutable milestone archive contains 196 verified files, SHA256 <code>e7ad31296caf8501fee2c04bac5765857a3cc3b8417b64f752ffd0960ed418de</code>. The seven retained serving code changes remain unchanged.</p><p>'''+reportlink('20260913_102428')+''' · <a href="att37-report.md">Result, profile limitations and recipe</a> · <a href="att37-dsa-split-lead.json">Per-rank sample counts</a> · <a href="att37-dsa-source-verification.json">Active source verification</a> · <a href="latency-att37.json">Reconstructed chart</a> · <a href="att37-snapshot-verification.json">Archive verification</a>.</p>''')
section('ten-k-result','ATT36: backlog regression and preserved milestone','''<div class="callout"><strong>Interrupted negative trial, valid generator.</strong> The guard stopped admissions after 213.8s. All 4,227 admitted requests succeeded; 7,615 were never admitted. Worst 20s TTFT p50 was 12.322s; 151/228 reconstructed windows exceeded 4s. No 600s performance pass is claimed.</div><p>Only three Prefill arguments changed: chunk, max-prefill and matching graph size 12K → 10K. The same seven source changes remain. Six canonical and four affinity checks and a 400-request warmup passed; both Prefills and all eight Decode DP caches were reset. New Prefill/session placement and a lighter status observer are additional comparison factors.</p><p>P151 slowed despite receiving fewer uncached tokens. At 90–120s, its mean forward was 1.622s and queue 7.614s, versus 0.977s / 1.346s on P132. All 107 logged P151 batches in that interval used 10K CUDA graphs. Only 1,846 / 4,227 matched requests retained their prior logical Prefill node. These counters and placement differences do not isolate the effect of chunk size.</p><p>Cache hit was 89.9445%; all 12,155 full 60s demand states within the partial admission span passed the recorded engineering bands. Store recorded 13 eviction passes and 818.09GB cumulative churn through closure. Generator lag p99 of 31.889ms passed the existing 50ms gate; its external OS samples showed no quota-throttle increments during their limited coverage. Kernel schedstats were disabled.</p><p><strong>Record finalized:</strong> 184 recipe/code/evidence files, every archived entry hash verified; SHA256 <code>1e568706a1af2d373f1ef3b4ed26cde332e187b16340981a0ab0c338a33405cb</code>. All 115 queue gauges drained and all collectors were joined. ATT37 subsequently repeated the imbalance with bounded CPU sampling; its closed result and capture limitations are recorded above. No new serving patch is claimed.</p><p>'''+reportlink('20260913_100538')+''' · <a href="att36-report.md">Result and recipe</a> · <a href="latency-att36.json">Raw chart reconstruction</a> · <a href="att36-placement-summary.json">Placement counts</a> · <a href="att36-stage-cache.json">Stage/cache observations</a> · <a href="att36-batch-shapes.json">Actual batch shapes</a> · <a href="att36-partial-load-cache.json">Partial demand audit</a> · <a href="att36-snapshot-verification.json">Verified archive</a>.</p>''')
section('generator-audit','CPU generator controls: closed evidence','''<p>Two isolated processes replayed all 11,842 saved requests and 35,526 callback events at their original timing offsets. Both used the actual live-controller and prefix-theory classes with the same bound Alex container and source hashes. GPUs were hidden, outbound connections denied, and no model requests were sent.</p>'''+table(['CPU-only diagnostic','Heartbeat p99','Heartbeat maximum','Snapshot maximum'],[
['One snapshot every 15s','10.860 ms','31.605 ms','21.739 ms'],['Three snapshots plus JSON encoding every 15s','10.570 ms','127.239 ms','46.084 ms'],
])+'''<p><strong>The full-test p99 was not reproduced.</strong> The isolated 127ms maximum is retained, but it does not establish the cause of ATT34/35's approximately 51ms p99. These controls omit HTTP uploads, SSE parsing, live file writes, the full scheduler and host CPU contention during GPU serving. Both finished all theory results, exited successfully and were joined.</p>
<p>Our former status poll could request three full snapshots every 15s. The prepared observer requests one while active and fetches complete detail after termination. Its terminal path reproduced ATT35's entire summary exactly. This changes our observation workload; it does not change application source, metrics or validation thresholds, and is not proven to fix generator lag; ATT36 passed, but changed workload duration and serving behavior limit attribution.</p>
<p><strong>Historical ATT36 decision amendment.</strong> Only Prefill chunk/max-prefill limits and matching graph size change from 12,288 to 10,240. Two Prefill workers roll; six other incarnations must remain fixed. The original prerequisite for a valid ATT35 baseline is preserved alongside an explicit amendment: invalid earlier measurements limit attribution, but do not prevent testing a new candidate. Final acceptance still requires a valid generator, exact load, zero errors and every 20s TTFT p50 below four seconds. Worker/session initial state and the lighter observer are additional comparison factors. Fresh bounded checks, cache reset and warmup preceded its measured trial; the closed negative result is recorded above.</p>
<p>The CPU archive contains 23 files, all entry hashes verified; SHA256 <code>6d4dbaaf1e302330796e36142c9e7e9ae2e0f614f38aaa6b707b9997dc4d332d</code>. <a href="generator-cpu-controls-report.md">CPU scope and limitations</a> · <a href="generator-cpu-controls-verification.json">Archive verification</a> · <a href="milestones.md">Milestones</a> · <a href="code-change-ledger.md">Code and configuration ledger</a>.</p>''')
section('repeat-result','ATT35: repeated delay; generator invalid','''<div class="callout"><strong>Second generator-invalid run; TTFT also misses the target.</strong> All 11,842 requests succeeded with zero failures and empty outputs. Event-loop lag p99 was 51.507188ms against the unchanged 50ms ceiling. Admission p99 37.206ms and body-send p99 46.741ms passed their separate limits. No accepted performance result is claimed.</div>
<p>All eight pod/container incarnations, serving source, images, resources, workload and validation limits remained unchanged. Fresh KV reset and a separate 400-request warmup preceded the full 600-second measurement. Existing bounded correctness checks were explicitly inherited from the identical runtime; no additional coverage is claimed.</p>'''+table(['ATT35 observation','Result'],[
['TTFT p50 / p90 / p99','3.370 / 4.546 / 5.659 s'],['Worst 20s p50 / failing windows','4.493 s at t=324; 60/602 above 4s'],['Measured cache hit / uncached tokens','89.877545% / 60,768,480'],['Full 60s demand windows','42,621 boundary/interior states; recorded engineering bands passed'],['Actual uncached 60s range','5,935,560–6,276,722 tokens'],['Store eviction churn','47 passes; 2.959 TB cumulative evicted bytes'],['Cold-cache warmup, separately recorded','400/400 success; TTFT p50 18.452 s'],
])+'''<p><strong>Session placement was retained.</strong> KV reset does not clear frontend session bindings. The repeat reused original session IDs inside the 1800-second idle TTL. Exact client-to-native-request joins show every measured request chose the same Prefill and distributed Decode worker as ATT34: 6,006 on P151 and 5,836 on P132. Decode DP rank is not exposed by that completion record. This is not a replication with newly assigned sessions.</p>
<p><strong>The hot cohort also exceeds four seconds in frontend timing.</strong> In ATT35's worst window, client p50 was 4.493s and frontend p50 4.430s. The median paired duration difference was 11.852ms. Their different timing boundaries prevent treating the difference as a network-only span, but the frontend result keeps service time and queueing central to the investigation.</p>
<p><strong>Initial closure decision:</strong> ATT36 was held pending a CPU audit. The controls and subsequent decision amendment are recorded above. Prefix-matching work and shared callback locks remain hypotheses, not established causes of the full-test lag. The generator threshold remains 50ms.</p>
<p>All 115 queue gauges drained, sources and identities matched, and every ATT35 collector was joined. The immutable milestone archive preserves 138 recipe/code/evidence files with every entry verified. TPOT tails and 53 lower-tier removal warnings remain recorded at the agreed lower priority.</p><p>'''+reportlink('20260913_090354')+''' · <a href="att35-report.md">Full recipe and result</a> · <a href="latency-att35.json">Reconstructed chart</a> · <a href="att35-workload-summary.json">Request accounting</a> · <a href="att35-rolling-load-cache.json">Rolling demand audit</a> · <a href="att35-routing-summary.json">Retained placement counts</a> · <a href="att35-client-frontend-ttft.json">Paired timing cohorts</a> · <a href="att35-stage-cache.json">Stage/cache counters</a> · <a href="att35-store-deltas.json">Store churn</a> · <a href="att35-snapshot-verification.json">Verified archive</a>.</p>''')
section('chunk-repeat','ATT34: 12K throughput and latency tradeoff','''<div class="callout"><strong>Generator invalid; this is not an accepted performance result.</strong> Event-loop lag p99 was 50.389651 ms against the unchanged 50 ms ceiling. Admission p99 37.373ms and body-send p99 47.117ms passed their separate limits; connector queue events were zero. All 11,842 requests succeeded, and all 115 queue gauges drained.</div>
<p>Only both Prefills changed from 8K to 12K chunks/max-prefill limits, adding the matching CUDA-graph size on every PP rank. Six other pod/container incarnations, all source patches, images, affinity 1800s / escape 0, eight-GPU Decode,1300 GiB Store and candidate05 workload remained fixed. No image was rebuilt and no serving code was added.</p>'''+table(['ATT34 observation','Result'],[
['TTFT p50 / p90 / p99','3.345 / 4.565 / 5.804 s'],['Worst 20s p50 / failing windows','4.571 s at t=457; 56/603 above 4s'],['ATT33 reference','6.116 s worst; 213/603 above 4s; valid generator'],['Measured cache hit / uncached tokens','89.875018% / 60,783,648'],['Full 60s demand windows','42,621 boundary/interior states; all within recorded engineering bands'],['Actual uncached 60s range','5,935,560–6,291,694 tokens'],['Store eviction churn','47 passes; 2.959 TB cumulative evicted bytes'],['Warmup, separately recorded','400/400 success; cold-cache TTFT p50 16.931s'],
])+'''<p>Raw timings reproduce every one of the 603 chart points. Early Prefill queues were smaller with 12K, while per-request forward, bootstrap and handoff counter means grew. This tradeoff motivates further work, but a valid unchanged repeat is needed before attributing the difference confidently. The 52 lower-tier-index warnings and deferred TPOT tails remain in the private evidence; an absent-block removal warning alone does not prove lost KV data.</p>
<p><strong>ATT35 subsequently repeated the exact 12K serving configuration; its invalid result and retained session state are recorded above.</strong> All eight runtime incarnations are retained. Fresh generator/token/payload attestation and cache reset precede the same 400-request warmup and 600-second measured schedule. Existing bounded-check results are explicitly inherited from the identical runtime; no new correctness coverage is claimed. Validation thresholds remain unchanged.</p><p>'''+reportlink('20260913_084212')+''' · <a href="att34-report.md">Full result and recipe</a> · <a href="latency-att34.json">Raw chart reconstruction</a> · <a href="att34-workload-summary.json">All-request accounting</a> · <a href="att34-rolling-load-cache.json">Rolling demand audit</a> · <a href="att34-stage-cache.json">Stage/cache counters</a> · <a href="att34-store-deltas.json">Store churn</a> · <a href="att34-snapshot-verification.json">Verified 156-file archive</a>.</p>''')
section('strict-affinity','ATT33: full load completed, Prefill queues remain','''<p>Two PP4/TP1 Prefills run on nodes 132 and 151. One TP8/DP8/EP8 Decode spans nodes 130 and 192; these are two physical pods of one distributed worker. Two 650 GiB Mooncake clients supply a private 1300 GiB shared cache. ATT33 retained 8K Prefill chunks and changed only frontend projected-load escape from 8000 ms to zero, with session affinity at 1800 seconds. Hard admission limits and external failure/backlog guards remained.</p>'''+table(['ATT33 measurement','Result'],[
['Admission / completion span','599.965 / 603.591 s'],['Successful requests / failures / empty outputs','11,842 / 0 / 0'],['Server input / cached / uncached tokens','600,333,408 / 539,642,176 / 60,691,232'],['Actual cache hit / finite-plan net deficit','89.890412% / 686,848 tokens'],['TTFT p50 / p90 / p99','3.773 / 5.247 / 6.920 s'],['Worst Alex20s TTFT p50','6.116 s at t=508; 395 samples'],['Windows above 4s p50','213 / 603; independently reconstructed'],['Load generator / terminal state','Valid; 115 idle gauges; all eight pod/container identities unchanged'],
])+'''<p><strong>Prefill queueing is the leading TTFT target.</strong> In 16 traces from the worst window, mean Prefill waiting was 3.647 s versus 0.571 s in eight control traces. Mean Prefill forward was 0.836 versus 0.776 s. These selected cohorts locate the delay; they are not a randomized causal estimate. Decode transfer-wait overlaps Prefill work and must not be added to those spans.</p>
<p><strong>L3 remains part of the investigation.</strong> Session affinity reduced host/shared-cache movement compared with ATT31, but the finite cache still churned. From the measured baseline to terminal idle, Store recorded 47 eviction passes and 2.958 TB of cumulative evicted bytes; cumulative eviction is not unique working-set size. Allocated bytes ended at 1.206 TB of 1.396 TB capacity. Keep actual GPU/host/L3 hits and misses distinct from the optimistic offline prefix model.</p>
<p>TPOT evidence is retained at lower priority: whole p99 19.616 ms, worst 20s p99 152.274 ms. The 24 sampled worst requests averaged 0.258 s in Decode forward and 2.270 s from scheduler completion to root-request completion. The exact later cause remains unproven. No new CPU profiling or correctness-research overlay was introduced.</p>
<p>Six canonical retrievals and four affinity checks passed before the fresh 400-request warmup. The exact candidate05 replay, source hashes, scoped cache resets, rollback and all negative outcomes remain saved. ATT34 changes only the two Prefills' chunk/max-prefill limits to 12288 and adds the matching graph size, to test throughput headroom.</p><p>'''+reportlink('20260913_075613')+''' · <a href="att33-report.md">Full reproduction record</a> · <a href="att33-workload-summary.json">Load/cache accounting</a> · <a href="latency-att33.json">Reconstructed latency</a> · <a href="strict-affinity-stage-cache.json">Stage/cache counters</a> · <a href="strict-affinity-store-deltas.json">Store churn</a> · <a href="strict-affinity-trace-summary.json">Trace-cohort summary</a>.</p>''')
