section('attempts','Diagnostics, failed approaches and retained history','''<p>The original phase covered 21 attempt directories and 18 completed ten-minute trials: 14 uninstrumented trials, four diagnostics, one interrupted diagnostic, one startup failure and one warmup-only anomaly. The preceding baseline is separate.</p>'''+table(['Attempt','Purpose / result'],[
['01','Bounded GPU diagnostic interrupted after profiler export disruption and a native-hash thread fault. Not an acceptance run; scoped Prefill recovery retained.'],
['02 / 03','Depth 1, then breakable CUDA graphs. Still accumulated backlog and rejected requests.'],
['04','CPU diagnostic: low OS runqueue wait weakened CPU scheduling starvation as the main explanation.'],
['05 / 06','Earlier control bundle, then depth 0. Depth 0 worsened sustained throughput.'],
['07 / 08','Launch before old-output handling, then enable breakable graphs on that source. Improvement, but still failures.'],
['09 / 10','Trace verbosity and 27-phase CPU timing diagnostics. Timing measures include synchronization waits.'],
['11','Earlier last-rank output: first full zero-failure run, but sustained TTFT still high.'],
['12','Earlier current-proxy publication failed startup through a lazy NCCL CPU-metadata wait cycle; rolled back.'],
['13','Control-safe proxy variant completed but regressed latency; excluded from best lineage.'],
['14 / 15','Early cached prefix and all-rank output relay tested separately. Prefix improved latency; all-rank relay alone did not.'],
['16 / 16b','Combined changes. First warmup had one missing-TTFT/empty-visible-output event; one predeclared fresh-reset retry completed. Original anomaly remains unresolved.'],
['17 / 18','Final-map reuse, then 30-phase diagnostic; page-map dependency wait motivated overlap work.'],
['19 / 20','Same-iteration map-copy overlap; unchanged fresh-cache repeat. Both pass the original 60s criterion, both retain shorter-window spikes.'],
])+'''<p>Historical counters recorded no quota throttling in the experiment containers or immediate pod parents. Sampled scheduler-main-thread runqueue wait was very small; this does not exclude locks, the GIL, synchronization or serial work. Initial queue growth was visible in Prefill before Decode saturation. Late Decode-forward means stayed near 0.2 seconds, while Prefill waiting grew markedly in early unsuccessful arms.</p>
<p>Observed bootstrap/final-transfer means in the final runs remain about 0.58 / 0.60 seconds. The original roughly 1.2-second handoff delays were reduced, not eliminated. The separate Decode-rejection cleanup issue was filed and deferred; successful runs do not prove it fixed.</p>''')
section('validation','Correctness checks and evidence limits','''<ul><li>51 CPU lifetime, payload and cursor checks; four deliberately unsafe variants rejected.</li><li>30 actual-loop ordering cases and two complete source/AST restoration checks.</li><li>Native CUDA copy semantics and graph/map-path activation on all four Prefill ranks.</li><li>Three long-context retrieval probes: two cold and one shared-prefix case. Final answers, payload hashes and input/cache counts matched. Reasoning text and output lengths varied; bitwise or token-level equivalence was not established.</li><li>Each final run: zero failures, no empty successful outputs, DONE observed, all TTFT values present, valid generator, 22 observed rejection/error counter series without increments, 56 queue/running gauges idle twice, three bound containers Ready with zero restarts.</li></ul>
<p>Correctness retrieval probes used up to 256 output tokens; the canonical performance workload remained capped at 20. Histories retain the failed short-budget probe and warmup anomaly. Missing counters remain unobserved, not zero. Trace requery recovered three later-visible spans; both query sets were saved. Startup evidence after log rotation was inherited only for the unchanged container, while current identities and source/spec hashes were rechecked.</p>''')
